UID:event_313841769@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031310Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T213000
SUMMARY:*IN-PERSON* SF/F Group
DESCRIPTION:Durham Writers Group\nWe will be at the People's Solidarity Hu
 b at 1809 Chapel Hill Rd\, Durham. This venue does not serve food or drink
 \, but feel free to bring your own. There is a kitchenette for our use\, b
 ut be sure to clean up afterwards. The space might be a little cozy\; plea
 se consider masking or staying home if you have a respiratory ailment.\n\n
 This sub-group focuses on Speculative Fiction\, including Science Fiction\
 , Fantasy and Horror. If you have anything that falls under that category 
 — be it short story\, poem\, novel-in-progress or screenplay — then co
 me! We'd love to hear from you.\n\nOur format allows each reader 15 minute
 s to present their work aloud\, followed by approximately 20 minutes of fe
 edback from the other attendees. To ensure fairness\, each attendee is lim
 ited to 1 minute of Initial Feedback time. During that period\, the author
  remains silent. Next\, we have a 5 minute Free-For-All discussion about t
 he work -- then the author may speak. (We usually get through three reader
 s.)\n\nThough not required\, in order to receive more in-depth feed-back\,
  readers may post their work in advance on our Google Group:\nhttps://grou
 ps.google.com/d/forum/durham-sff-writers-group\n\nWe ask that participants
  keep their comments constructive and respectful\, focusing on what works 
 or doesn't work in the piece.\n\nWe also ask that readers provide a warnin
 g\, both on the Google Group and during the meeting\, if their story featu
 res content that some readers might find upsetting. This includes descript
 ions of violence or sexual content.\n\nReaders are:\n• Milbre\n• Ryan\
 n• Abigail\n\nBackup Readers are:\n• Baxter\n• Sigma\n• James\n\nD
 eep Backup:\n• Fabian\n\n***\n\n***We meet every Tuesday at the same tim
 e\, but alternate between In-Person*** ***and on Zoom. Members may attend 
 both formats\, if desired\, but readers will be listed separately under th
 e In-Person or Zoom weeks.***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/dwg-writers/events/313841769/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260318T230826Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260318T230826Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unitedarts": "https://unitedarts.org/calendar/beer-and-banjos-the-holland-brothers-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unitedarts
X-SOURCE:United Arts Wake County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260407T210000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231216
CREATED:20260401T182034Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T192538Z
UID:10007466-1775586600-1775595600@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:Beer and Banjos: The Holland Brothers
DESCRIPTION:From the Piedmont region of North Carolina\, the Holland Brothers play a style of music rooted in old-school country and country blues\, with close harmonies and blues harmonica. Drawing inspiration from Charlie Poole to Charlie Patton\, from Muddy Waters to the Memphis Jug Band\, from the country gospel sounds of Flatt and Scruggs and the Louvin Brothers\, from the high lonesome sound of Bill Monroe\, or from the pairing of Woody Guthrie and Cisco Houston\, the brothers have appeared in publications and events such as No Depression\, Our State\, the North Carolina State Fair\, Billboard Magazine\, and the New York Times and continue to garner praise and gain new fans daily. Learn more about the Holland Brothers here. \nBeer and Banjos is a free\, family-friendly evening of roots music every Tuesday at Raleigh’s Bowstring Pizza and Brewyard. Hosted by the mighty local musicians known collectively as the Beer and Banjos Allstars\, these weekly concerts feature guest musicians and take place on Bowstring’s spacious patio when the weather allows\, or inside by the bar when rain\, heat\, or cold threaten the vibe. \nTips for the musicians are gratefully accepted (look for a helper walking around with a bucket for cash and QR codes for online tips)\, and don’t forget to check out the merch table. Bowstring serves tasty pizza and other food as well as cold beer and other beverages. \nLearn more about Beer and Banjos events statewide here.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/beer-and-banjos-the-holland-brothers-3/
LOCATION:Bowstring Pizza and Brewyard\, 1930 Wake Forest Rd\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27608\, United States
CATEGORIES:Beer and Banjos
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Holland-Bros-BB-2026-169-for-event-DLOefn.png
END:VEVENT
