X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Community Events
DESCRIPTION:NC State’s annual Take Back the Night is an event that reclaims
  the night and our campus for survivors of sexual assault. Join us at Staff
 ord Commons for a resource fair at 4 p.m. and the main program at 5 p.m. A 
 rally and a march across campus will follow. The evening will culminate in 
 a powerful Survivor Speak Out at Talley Student Union in the Currituck-Hatt
 eras Ballroom immediately following the march. Counselors will be available
  for private counseling in the Ocracoke Ballroom in Talley during the speak
  out. The evening will conclude with a gathering at the Women’s Center in T
 alley that will include food\, healing and community building.\n\nTake Back
  the Night is part of the university's Sexual Assault Awareness Month obser
 vance in April. Please visit the Women's Center website to learn about more
  events happening during Sexual Assault Awareness Month.
DTEND:20260409T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030230Z
DTSTART:20260408T200000Z
GEO:35.783848;-78.670939
LOCATION:Stafford Commons
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Take Back the Night
