BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Unitedarts": "https://unitedarts.org/calendar/the-road-through-dont-ask-dont-tell/2026-04-09/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:unitedarts
X-SOURCE:United Arts Wake County
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T220000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231216
CREATED:20260120T155524Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260120T155524Z
UID:10006513-1775725200-1775772000@unitedarts.org
SUMMARY:The Road Through “Don’t Ask\, Don’t Tell”
DESCRIPTION:The Road Through Don’t Ask\, Don’t Tell by photographer\, oral historian\, and U.S. Marine Corps veteran Theresa Scott. This deeply personal documentary exhibition explores the lived experiences of LGBTQIA+ veterans who served under restrictive military policies. \nThrough intimate portrait photography paired with first-person oral histories\, Scott brings forward stories long silenced by institutional policy and cultural pressure. Drawing on her own service\, she offers viewers an unflinching look at the realities faced by service members who were expected to serve with honor while hiding essential parts of who they were. \nExhibition Dates: February 1 – April 26\, 2026\nArtist Talk & Reception: March 26\, 5:30–7:00 p.m.
URL:https://unitedarts.org/calendar/the-road-through-dont-ask-dont-tell/2026-04-09/
LOCATION:Pullen Arts Center
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://unitedarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/DADT-24.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Pullen Arts Center":MAILTO:pullenartscenter@raleighnc.gov
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_b32e7018b18e1a8650f0d178e5d8314fd6664c368233eead570b44e368f882c9
SUMMARY:Right to Be's Bystander Intervention to Stop Online Harassment: Ho
 w to Be an Ally When You Witness Abuse Online
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T103000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031320Z
UID:3fnor8f6fot1rib828o0036j8p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T100000
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20260104T011835Z
DESCRIPTION:REGISTER HERE: <a href="https://righttobe.org/events/bystande
 r-intervention-to-stop-online-harassment-how-to-be-an-ally-when-you-witnes
 s-abuse-online-7/">https://righttobe.org/events/bystander-intervention-to-
 stop-online-harassment-how-to-be-an-ally-when-you-witness-abuse-online-7/<
 /a> <br><br><section><br><br><br><p>PEN America and Right to Be have part
 nered to provide training on how to intervene safely when you see a journa
 list attacked online. This training is also brought to you in partnership 
 with the NYC Commission on Gender Equity\, the Mayor’s Office of Equity 
 and Racial Justice\, and the NYC Commission on Gender Equity.</p><br><p>In
  this free\, one-hour\, interactive training\, we’ll give you the tools 
 you need to intervene safely and effectively in online abuse using Right T
 o Be’s 5Ds of bystander intervention. First\, we’ll talk through what 
 online harassment is and how to identify abusive tactics. We’ll discuss 
 the severe impact online abuse can have – on well being\, livelihoods\, 
 and free expression – and how it’s drowning out voices that urgently n
 eed to be heard in public discourse. Then\, we’ll share concrete strateg
 ies for how to distract\, delegate\, document\, delay\, or directly interv
 ene in a way that is safe\, effective\, and centered on the needs of the p
 erson being targeted.</p><p>We’ll have time to practice so you can leave
  feeling more confident intervening the next time you see someone being ab
 used online. We hope you’ll join us to learn how we can all band togethe
 r to do your part to protect press freedom and defend the media from attac
 ks on their independence\, including online abuse and threats.</p></sectio
 n><section><br><br></section>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260104T011835Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (Virtual US)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-stories-4-2026-04-09/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T113000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231147
CREATED:20220420T195217Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260401T003440Z
UID:111838-1775730600-1775734200@naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Nature Stories – CANCELLED
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we open your eyes to the wonderful world of nature through a family-friendly\, nature-filled storytime. We’ll begin by sharing a story in the Nature PlaySpace Amphitheater at 10:30am\, and will then head to other areas of Prairie Ridge as we explore natural themes from each day’s stories in a hands-on\, interactive manner. \nThis is a free program beginning at 10:30am. Come dressed for the weather and prepared to take a walk! Most walks will be stroller friendly. Everyone is welcome at the Nature PlaySpace\, but it has been designed especially for kids 7 and younger.  Nature Stories books and activities were chosen with this age group in mind. \nPlease note that this program occurs at the Museum’s Prairie Ridge Ecostation location in west Raleigh. For more information\, contact prairieridge@naturalsciences.org
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-stories-4-2026-04-09/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Children,Nature Stories,Outdoor Experiences
ORGANIZER;CN="Emma%20Blackford":MAILTO:emma.blackford@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.812182885871;-78.713963528554
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Prairie Ridge 1671 Gold Star Drive Raleigh NC 27607 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=1671 Gold Star Drive:geo:-78.713963528554,35.812182885871
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-minds-adventure-scavenger-hunt"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Homeschool & Education Days,Exhibits & Tours,
 Special Site Programs,Outdoor & Recreation,Outdoor Recreation (kayak, paddl
 e, hikes),Nature & Wildlife Programs,Youth & Family Activities
DESCRIPTION:Join the Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt at Elk Knob Sta
 te Park. Journey through northern hardwood forest\, follow winding mountain
  trails\, and explore the unique ecosystems of this high-elevation park. Ke
 ep your eyes open—what signs of wildlife or weather-shaped landscapes will 
 you uncover? Look for unique rocks that make Elk Knob a very special clue i
 n North Carolina’s geologic history. Start at the Visitor Center and scan t
 he QR code in your Actionbound app. Flyers with the QR code will be placed 
 in the Park Office and on all park map kiosks. \n\nThe adventures are avail
 able on the Actionbound app – a free download to your cellphone through you
 r phone’s app store. There’s no need to create a profile and no personal da
 ta is collected with Actionbound. You simply find new hunts by searching fo
 r the park name or scanning the associated QR code posted for your park’s a
 dventure.\n\nThis program is made possible through a partnership with the N
 C Science Trail (ncsciencetrail.org)! Visit their website for more Curious 
 Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunts being held in other NC State Parks and for 
 other programs being offered throughout the state. \n\nThis scavenger hunt 
 is running now through April 30\, 2026.
DTEND:20260410T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030451Z
DTSTART:20260409T110000Z
GEO:36.333462;-81.696432
LOCATION:Elk Knob State Park
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Elk Knob State Park: Curious Minds Adventure Scavenger Hunt
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52374989490813
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/elk-knob-state-park-curious-minds-adve
 nture-scavenger-hunt
END:VEVENT
