SUMMARY:Play Board Games at the Geekery
DESCRIPTION:Triangle Board Games and Bars\nCome play games at Gamers Geeke
 ry and Tavern every thursday night!\n\nStarting time is 6:30\, but feel fr
 ee to come in anytime and just hang out for the night. Group is very casua
 l and friendly.\n\nHow it works:\nCome on in\, grab a name tag and pay the
  $2.50 meetup participant fee at the bar area\, find the tables that are r
 eserved for the Meetup group\, play games with others who show up. Food an
 d drinks are available at the bar.\n\nPlease RSVP by noon day of. If less 
 than four people are able to attend a given Wednesday the event will be ca
 nceled.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/triangle-board-games-and-bars/events/
 313874760/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260320T231915Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260320T231915Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/salamanders-of-the-piedmont-monroe/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T193000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231201
CREATED:20260327T150701Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260327T150702Z
UID:10001555-1775759400-1775763000@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Salamanders of the Piedmont (Monroe)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Union County Wildlife chapter to learn all about salamanders from Dr. Kira McEntire! Dr. McEntire is an assistant professor at Queens University of Charlotte. She has been doing research on amphibians and reptiles for over 10 years\, with a focus on salamander ecology and behavior. Her research includes monitoring a population of marbled salamanders and their breeding behavior and exploring the color variation of Cope’s gray treefrogs. During this program she will share with us the ecology and conservation of local species. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/salamanders-of-the-piedmont-monroe/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/UCWCsalamanders.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/gardening-for-the-planet-greensboro/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260409T203000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231201
CREATED:20260302T173318Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260302T173319Z
UID:10001507-1775759400-1775766600@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Gardening for the Planet (Greensboro)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Triad Wild! Chapter for a joint event with T. Gilbert Pearson Audubon Society at the SAIL Center at the Greensboro Science Center. We will be screening the documentary Gardening for the Planet\, which shows how something as simple as the plants you chose for your garden can be impactful in the struggle to combat climate change. This film will leave you with a sense of hope by showing how even one person can improve the ecosystem in their tiny part of the planet by planting native plants. For those who still want to achieve a landscaped look in their lawn\, the film also demonstrates that this style is still possible while opting for native plants. Join us for an uplifting documentary screening! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/gardening-for-the-planet-greensboro/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/planet.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/create-your-own-library-a-book-binding-and-bookstagram-workshop"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training,Community Events,Student Life
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center (AACC) for a hands-on
  workshop to learn how to bookbind\, have community conversations and start
  building a library of your thoughts\, stories and reading reflections. Lib
 rarian Beatrice Downey will begin the workshop with a short presentation on
  sustaining reading as a lifelong habit and recording your reading journeys
  through journaling and Instagram. Participants will create a collage with 
 fun materials\, images of Black student life at NC State provided by the Sp
 ecial Collections Research Center and quotes from Black authors curated by 
 the African American Cultural Center's librarian.\n\nAttendees will meet ar
 chivists and preservationists from the Special Collections Research Center 
 and get a glimpse into their careers.\n\nStudent attendees will have a chan
 ce to win one of two Patron prize kits containing limited-edition AACC Libr
 ary swag\, a free book\, library starter materials and more.\n\nThe worksho
 p is part of the AACC's celebration of National Library Week.
DTEND:20260409T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030230Z
DTSTART:20260409T190000Z
GEO:35.787562;-78.669711
LOCATION:D.H. Hill Jr. Library\, Fishbowl Forum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Create Your Own Library: A Book Binding and Bookstagram Workshop
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52456319776697
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/create-your-own-library-a-book-binding-
 and-bookstagram-workshop
END:VEVENT
