CATEGORIES:
DESCRIPTION:Project WET: Foundations of Water Education is an interdiscipli
 nary water science training program for formal and nonformal educators of K
 -12 students. It focuses on all things water\, including physical character
 istics\, environmental characteristics\, water's social and cultural import
 ance\, and more. Experience firsthand the diversity of North Carolina's wat
 er resources and discover new ideas for teaching about water in both the cl
 assroom and the field. The Curriculum Guide is full of standards-aligned\, 
 hands-on activities. Email marissa.blackburn@ncparks.gov to register.
DTEND:20260410T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260410T130000Z
