BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/opening-day-exhibit-battlefields-to-backwoods-soldiers-shaping-appalachia"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Education Programs,Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a powerful new exhibit celebrating America’s 250th 
 anniversary. This immersive display explores how Revolutionary War veterans
 \, including Transylvania's own Patriots such as Lambert Clayton\, transiti
 oned into pioneers in the former Cherokee lands that would one day become T
 ransylvania County. The exhibit highlights land grants\, frontier skills\, 
 and lasting legacies\, all tying back to the fight for independence. \n\nCo
 mplementing the exhibit is our Revolutionary Era Garden\, established in 20
 25 with support from the Transylvania County 250th Committee and America 25
 0 NC\, where families can engage in hands-on activities while learning abou
 t Colonial life and our Founding Fathers.\n\nThe exhibit will open in April
  and run through mid-October. Free and open to all.
DTEND:20260411T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260411T040000Z
GEO:35.23255;-82.731022
LOCATION:Transylvania Heritage Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Opening Day– Exhibit: Battlefields to Backwoods-Soldiers Shaping Ap
 palachia
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52390740567581
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/opening-day-exhibit-battlefields-to-ba
 ckwoods-soldiers-shaping-appalachia
END:VEVENT
