CREATED:20260320T193842Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>BIRD OUTING: <strong>Birding With Frank at Turnipseed Natur
 e Preserve</strong></p><p>Bird Outing on <strong>SATURDAY APRIL 11\, 2026\
 , 8:30 am TO 10:00 am</strong></p><p>Location: <strong>Turnipseed Nature P
 reserve</strong> has TWO entrances. We meet at <strong>1525 Pleasants Road
 \, Wendell.</strong></p><p>Leader is Frank Doherty ( fdoherty@nc.rr.com )<
 /p><p>This birdwalk repeats on the second Saturday of most months. Check M
 eetup and wakeaudubon.org calendars for updates\; We temporarily moved fro
 m Wendell Park because it is a vital and very busy park for sports.</p><p>
 Turnipseed is a newer acquisition in the Raleigh preserve system\, with no
  sports other than nature study.</p><p></p><p>Park in the lot on Pleasants
  Road and look for people with binoculars. If you find yourself at the wro
 ng entrance\, then you can try walking the single gravel trail and maybe c
 atch up.</p><p></p><p>Turnipseed ebird hotspot: <a href="https://ebird.org
 /hotspot/L5052420">https://ebird.org/hotspot/L5052420</a></p><p></p><p>Tha
 nks\, Frank\, for volunteering to be the trip leader!</p><p></p><p>Thank y
 ou for your interest in birding with others. Our Meetup is FREE to you and
  supported by Wake Audubon. We hope you will support us by joining Wake Au
 dubon Society ($20 per year) and by donations and by volunteering. See <a 
 href="http://wakeaudubon.org/support/">http://wakeaudubon.org/support/</a>
  for more information.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T213159Z
LOCATION:Wendell Park\, West 3rd Street\, Wendell\, NC
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Wake Audubon
END:VEVENT
