SUMMARY:Wild Ideas: You Are A Force For Nature
DESCRIPTION:Save the date! Wild Ideas April 2026\nTLC invites you to join us at the NC Museum of Art for our annual Wild Ideas event! This year\, community partners and TLC staff will host a series of family-friendly activities that intersect art with the environment and celebrate how we can all be forces for nature. \nVisit the art museum park from 10:00am-2:00pm on April 11th to meet local organizations doing amazing work to provide opportunities to enjoy the outdoors and have a positive impact on local natural habitats. The Museum of Art will also host a morning volunteer workday to support their creek watershed restoration project!  More details and a schedule of events will be posted on our Wild Ideas website soon. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required. \n\nLearn more!
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/wildideas26
LOCATION:NC Museum of Art\, 1950 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_wakeaudubon
SUMMARY:Volunteer: Creek Trash Trap
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260411T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260411T123000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031314Z
UID:7ctj182gn9fq72dt35pu9fd7a1@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260411T103000
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260325T004745Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>Volunteer: Creek Trash Trap</b><br>In coordination with Sou
 nd Rivers\, Wake Audubon has adopted the<b> Little Rock Creek Trash Trap a
 t Walnut Creek </b> for<br>the month of April. We would love your help wi
 th our cleanout event on April 11th  from 10:30 to 12:30 at the Walnut Cr
 eek Wetland Center\, <br>950 Peterson St\, Raleigh\, NC 27610<br><br>Plea
 se go to the<br>following Activate Good link for details and to register.<
 br><a href="https://volunteer.activategood.org/opportunities/G3NiXYSFgv" t
 arget="_blank">https://volunteer.activategood.org/opportunities/G3NiXYSFgv
 </a><br><p>Cleaning out a<b> trash trap</b> (a barrier that catches litter
  n a stream) gives groups the chance to monitor the amount of trash collec
 ted by a trash trap\, organize clean-outs and participate in keeping local
  waterways clean.</p>Your involvement will positively impact the environme
 nt by reducing pollution within our waterways\, protecting wildlife from h
 armful trash ingestion and increasing water quality for both humans and wi
 ldlife.<br><br>Participants will work together to remove trash within the 
 trash trap and along the streambank.  All trash will be weighed and the da
 ta reported back to Sound Rivers.  Trash grabbers\, collection supplies\, 
 waders\, and snacks will be provided.<br><br>Waterproof Boots or old sneak
 ers recommended.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T005952Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Wake Audubon
END:VEVENT
