DESCRIPTION:Are you new to native plant gardening or looking to deepen your
  knowledge of native plants? Join staff from the Library of North Carolina’
 s Government and Heritage Library and the NC Museum of Natural Sciences for
  a Native Plant Walk and Planting Workshop on April 11 from 10 am to noon.\
 n\nLauri Lawson\, horticulturalist and native plant expert\, will lead a to
 ur of the native plant gardens at North Carolina Department of Natural and 
 Cultural Resources sites on East Jones Street\, including the DNCR building
  and the North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences.\n\nThis event will prim
 arily take place outdoors\, with participants traveling approximately ½ mil
 e round-trip via paved sidewalks.\n\nRegistration is requested:  https://fs
 25.formsite.com/statelibrarync/0426plantwalk/index\n\n Questions about this
  event? Contact us at ghl.info@dncr.nc.gov.\n\nThis event is hosted in conn
 ection with the GHL's Native Plant Seed Library. Learn more about our seed 
 library at slnc.info/seeds.
