BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260412T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260412T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207082933451
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_enoriver_org_9u7o786v1jlk6heq5cp3k1gr1k
SUMMARY:ERA - Guided Wildflower Hike - Confluence Natural Area
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260412T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260412T160000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031316Z
UID:1c92soapd2a9nf53je29mtvign@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260412T140000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260219T160743Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><u><u><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/1984072603567?a
 ff=oddtdtcreator" target="_blank">Registration is required</a></u></u> - 
 Tickets drop on March 1st at 8:00am!<br>Price: $4<br>*Ticket prices direct
 ly support the work of the Eno River Association. Thank you for your suppo
 rt!</p><p><br></p><p>This guided hike will explore various trails at the C
 onfluence\, based on where the best spring blooms are at the time. The Con
 fluence is a magical place for spring wildflowers!</p><p><br></p><p>Meet a
 t the pavilion beside the parking lot. This hike will take approximately t
 wo hours (sometimes less\, sometimes more). Please feel free to bring wate
 r and snacks. Wear comfortable\, weather-appropriate clothing and shoes. W
 ell-behaved dogs are welcome as long as they are under your control and on
  a 6-foot leash. Restrooms are available on-site.</p><p><br></p><p>The add
 ress is 4214 Highland Farm Rd\, Hillsborough\, NC 27278.</p><p>From Hillsb
 orough take Hwy 86 North away from town 1.6 miles from US70. Turn left on 
 Coleman Loop 1.1 miles. Turn left on Highland Farm Rd 2.4 miles. The Confl
 uence is on the left. There is a large sign and a gravel driveway. From no
 rthern Orange County take Hwy 86 south after passing Walnut Grove Church R
 d take the first right on Kenion Rd 1.7 miles. Turn right on Highland Farm
  Rd 0.6 miles. The Confluence is on the left. There is a large sign and a 
 gravel driveway.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260226T182716Z
LOCATION:4214 Highland Farm Rd\, Hillsborough\, NC 27278\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Eno River Association
END:VEVENT
