BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:NHBA Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260415T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260415T103000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031314Z
UID:33tn57psl4mff3u7g29g0n9hq6@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260415T073000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260328T001907Z
DESCRIPTION:Contact Tom Driscoll at <a href="mailto:spttdrdshnk@yahoo.com
 " target="_blank">spttdrdshnk@yahoo.com</a>  with questions. The location
  will be Transis Camp Road (aka Old Hope Valley Farm Road)\, Chapel Hill\,
  NC.  Note there may be no road sign for the turn but there is a brown ga
 me lands sign across Farrington Road from the turn. There are no other tur
 ns nearby so if you think you&#39\;re close\, that&#39\;s it. When you hav
 e gone about a mile\, the road will take a 90-degree right turn and there 
 is a large parking lot on the left. We will meet there (35 51 37 N\, 78 59
  26.25 W). An old but good description including directions <a href="https
 ://www.google.com/url?q=http://tbg.carolinanature.com/ohvfr.html&amp\;sa=D
 &amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0XfE1_RO19cE-Q-HkiM4cQ" ta
 rget="_blank">can be found here</a>.<br><br>This outing is sponsored by th
 e New Hope Bird Alliance (formerly New Hope Audubon).<br><br>Outings usual
 ly last 2-3 hours. No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a large 
 turnout for any particular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do re
 commend carpooling for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, ther
 e is a ‘no-pet’ policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of al
 l skill levels are welcome. <br><br>Please wear long pants\, socks\, and 
 sturdy shoes (ticks and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protection a
 re also recommended. Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain will r
 esult in cancellation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260328T001907Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/lifelong-hike-howell-woods-birding/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260415T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260415T170000
DTSTAMP:20260406T231147
CREATED:20260129T165040Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260303T174454Z
UID:117956-1776240000-1776272400@naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Lifelong Hike: Howell Woods Birding
DESCRIPTION:Birds will be our focus on this special birding experience at Howell Woods. Located in southeastern Johnston County\, Howell Woods is a 2800-acre natural area owned and managed by Johnston Community College for educational and recreational purposes. After an indoor introductory session\, Howell Woods staff and guest biologists will lead our exploration of some of the diverse habitats in search of birds. \nPlease note: You will be required to enter the following information for each registrant before you can complete your registration: emergency contact\, physician contact and health information (allergies\, conditions\, medications relevant to this field experience). Take a moment to gather this information before beginning your registration. \nREGISTRATION FOR THIS TRIP IS FULL \nIf the trip is full\, please email Missy Chernick to be added to the waitlist. \nRegistration deadline: Monday\, April 13 at 8:00 AM \nFor additional information about this trip and other Lifelong Hikes & Adventures\, contact Jerry Reynolds at 919.707.9884.
URL:https://naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/lifelong-hike-howell-woods-birding/
LOCATION:In the Field
CATEGORIES:Adults,Lifelong Learners,Outdoor Experiences,Trips
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
