X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/architecture-lecture-andrew-e-thompson"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
DESCRIPTION:Please join the College of Design for the spring 2026 architect
 ure lecture series. This is the AIA Triangle Design Award Jury Chair Lectur
 e. \n\nAndrew E. Thompson\, Preservation NJ\n\nServing in his first term on
  the Preservation New Jersey Board is Andrew E. Thompson\, who has been in 
 the field of architecture for 30 years. His education includes City Univers
 ity of New York\, the Pratt Institute\, and Columbia University.\n\nAndrew’
 s extensive career includes designing structural components for the Arleigh
  Burke Class Navy Destroyer vessel\; the Port Authority – working on projec
 ts in Tower One of the World Trade Center\, Newark Airport\, and the Air Tr
 ain for JFK airport\; Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center where he serve
 d as the Chief Architect\; and the City University of New York\, where he w
 as responsible for building their first new community college in 40 years. 
 In 2013\, Andrew came to New Jersey taking the position of County Architect
  for Passaic County.
DTEND:20260416T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260415T223000Z
GEO:35.787841;-78.638157
LOCATION:AIA NC Center for Architecture and Design
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Architecture Lecture: Andrew E. Thompson\, Preservation NJ
