BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/two-lights-for-tomorrow-2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Two Lights for Tomorrow' Will Shine in Communities Across Bruns
 wick County Friday\, April 18\n\n \n\nAs we approach the 250th anniversary 
 of the signing of the Declaration of Independence in 2026\, Brunswick Count
 y residents are requested to participate in a powerful moment of reflection
  and unity and to honor the spirit of cooperation and courage that helped i
 gnite the American Revolution.\n\nOn the night of April 18\, 1775\, Paul Re
 vere and William Dawes rode out from Boston to alert their fellow patriots 
 of the movement of the British regulars. A prearranged signal — two lantern
 s in the tower of Christ Church — warned that the British troops were trave
 ling via the Charles River. Other riders joined Revere and Dawes\, creating
  a network across the Massachusetts countryside which eventually led to the
  NC/SC border where a rider informed Isaac Marion\, proprietor of the Bound
 ary House and brother of Swamp Fox Francis Marion.\n\nLaunched in 2025\, Tw
 o Lights for Tomorrow was initiated by America 250 NC to encourage communit
 ies across North Carolina to illuminate two lights on notable buildings and
  homes\, commemorating the renowned ride through the colonies.\n\nBrunswick
  Town Chapter NSDAR continues that effort on Friday\, April 18\, 2026\, as 
 we urge businesses and homes throughout the county to shine two lights on t
 heir structures or in windows.
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260418
LOCATION:
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Two Lights for Tomorrow 2026
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52365668080596
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/two-lights-for-tomorrow-2026
END:VEVENT
