BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/celebrating-our-colonial-roots-online-plant-sale"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:The Brunswick County Master Gardeners Volunteer Association wil
 l hold an online plant sale starting on April 17\, 2026 and running until A
 pril 24\, 2026 with pick up day on May 1\, 2026. This event celebrates the 
 important colonial history of Brunswick County  through education on herbs\
 , flowers\, vines\, shrubs and small trees which thrive here. Plants featur
 ed are those which our Colonial ancestors would have encountered along our 
 coast and the Cape Fear River which are native to our region and support po
 llinators. Also featured will be plants from seeds which colonists brought 
 with them from Europe and plants which recognize the contributions and life
  celebrations of the Gullah Geechee people who were enslaved in Africa to w
 ork the rice plantations along the Cape Fear River. This online plant sale 
 celebrates the cultural traditions  found in gardening in our coastal regio
 n of the State.
DTEND:20260419T130000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260418T130000Z
GEO:34.056715;-78.165769
LOCATION:Pick up 5/1/26 at Greenhouses behind Building N
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Celebrating Our Colonial Roots - Online Plant Sale
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_50921813033727
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/celebrating-our-colonial-roots-online-
 plant-sale
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-on-display"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Organizational,Celebrations & Comme
 morations,Ceremonies & Anniversaries,Open Houses
DESCRIPTION:You are invited to explore the history of Davie County as the S
 emiquincentennial draws closer. There will be historical artifacts on displ
 ay representing the county's history. This includes a portrait of Continent
 al Army Colonel William R. Davie\, the county's namesake. There's also a lo
 t of information on Daniel Boone\, who lived in Davie County for seven year
 s. His parents are buried in Mocksville's Joppa Cemetery. Feel free to brow
 se around the room and examine historical records and documents\, including
  a list of those who served during the American Revolution. \n\nThese artif
 acts and documents are located inside the Martin-Wall History Room within t
 he Davie County Public Library in Mocksville. This room acts as the Davie C
 ounty history museum. Paying a visit will allow you to explore the county's
  long and proud history while gaining a better understanding of the Semiqui
 ncentennial's significance. These artifacts will be on display from Monday\
 , March 16\, until at least Sunday\, July 6.
DTEND:20260418T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260418T130000Z
GEO:35.897815;-80.5597
LOCATION:Davie County Public Library\, Martin-Wall History Room
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:History on Display
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52372920375106
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-on-display
END:VEVENT
