BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/art2wear-open-studio"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Community Events
DESCRIPTION:Students in the Art2Wear studio will offer a behind-the-scenes 
 look at what goes into making this annual show so iconic. Join us for a opp
 ortunity to see the student designers at work\, ask them questions and see 
 the details that make up their final collections. \n\nArt2WearTM (A2W) is a
 n educational event where students gain experience by coordinating and prod
 ucing an annual wearable art production. Young designers are challenged to 
 imagine\, create and inspire by expressing their point of view through wear
 able art. This highly anticipated show fuses the talents of several departm
 ents in the College of Design and beyond\, exposing student designers to th
 e broader fields of wearable art\, digital media production and fashion. A2
 W attracts attendees from all over the Triangle by encouraging participatio
 n through engaging the student body\, the Raleigh community and the broader
  design industry.
DTEND:20260421T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260421T200000Z
GEO:35.785182;-78.667643
LOCATION:Leazar Hall\, 325A
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Art2Wear: Open Studio 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52505794380808
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/art2wear-open-studio
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/fashion-week-film-screening-artist-talk-whose-woods-are-these"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Films
DESCRIPTION:Please attend a screening of Whose Woods Are These\, a seven-mi
 nute animated short created entirely from woven fabric by Associate Profess
 or Kate Nartker. Presented as part of the NC State  Fashion Week\, this spe
 cial event marks a full-circle moment as the film returns to NC State follo
 wing a year-long festival run.\n\nThe animation is composed of jacquard-wov
 en textiles that were scanned and sequenced frame by frame\, transforming c
 loth into a moving image. Inspired by a 19th-century family story set in no
 rthwest Ohio’s Great Black Swamp\, the film reimagines themes of disappeara
 nce\, wilderness and wonder through a tactile\, fiber-based lens.\n\nFollow
 ing the screening\, Nartker will share a brief presentation on the weaving 
 and animation process and the story that inspired the work.  Nartker will a
 lso answer questions.
DTEND:20260421T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260421T200000Z
GEO:35.769292;-78.676638
LOCATION:James B. Hunt Jr. Library\, Teaching and Visualization Lab
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fashion Week Screening and Artist Talk: Whose Woods Are These 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52391080463455
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/fashion-week-film-screening-artist-talk
 -whose-woods-are-these
END:VEVENT
