BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/kiana-bonollo-how-i-built-a-fashion-career-using-social-media"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Lectures and Talks
DESCRIPTION:What began as posting sewing projects on YouTube evolved into a
  multi-platform business built on digital sewing patterns\, online educatio
 n and brand partnerships. In this talk\, Kiana Bonollo '21\, a content crea
 tor and patternmaker\, will discuss how she identified a gap in the market\
 , listened to her audience and turned technical design skills into scalable
  digital products.\n\nShe will explore how social media has transformed ent
 repreneurship in the fashion industry: lowering marketing barriers\, creati
 ng direct access to consumers and opening new career paths beyond tradition
 al corporate roles. Students will learn how to think strategically about so
 cial platforms\, whether as influencers\, entrepreneurs or designers buildi
 ng their own brands.\n\nThe event is free but has limited capacity. Registr
 ation is required. NC State students and employees have priority registrati
 on (open now!). Registration will be open to the public on April 13 if spot
 s remain.
DTEND:20260421T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260421T220000Z
GEO:35.770005;-78.67824
LOCATION:Wilson College of Textiles\, W. Duke Kimbrell Atrium
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Kiana Bonollo: How I Built a Fashion Career Using Social Media
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52189714235233
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/kiana-bonollo-how-i-built-a-fashion-car
 eer-using-social-media
