BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Rdu Artificial Intelligence Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/all-things-ai-live/events/314147027/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_rdu_artificial_intelligence_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Meetup: All Things AI
UID:event_314147027@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031311Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260422T193000
SUMMARY:Building Your Startup in the Age of AI
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\n*This session is presented by [All Thing
 s AI](https://allthingsai.org) in partnership with [The American Undergrou
 nd](https://americanunderground.com) at the American Tobacco Campus as par
 t of [Raleigh Durham Startup Week](https://www.raleighdurhamstartupweek.co
 m).*\n\nMark Hinkle has been in and around startups for most of his career
 . Cloud.com — acquired by Citrix for $300 million. TriggerMesh — co-fo
 unded it\, backed by Index Ventures and Cisco. A handful of others that ne
 ver made the headlines\, and honestly\, most don't. That's the nature of t
 he game. You raise capital\, you hire people\, you try to get leverage\, a
 nd then you race against the clock until you either win or you don't.\n\nT
 hat model is changing. Fast.\n\nSam Altman has said that someday we'll see
  a single-person billion-dollar company. That may be further out than the 
 hype cycle suggests — but what's happening right now is this: a 10-perso
 n company with hundreds\, maybe thousands\, of AI agents working around th
 e clock is not science fiction. It's a capital strategy.\nThe question isn
 't whether AI changes how startups are built. It already has. The question
  is what founders do with that leverage\, and how they get started.\n\nIn 
 this session\, Mark will walk through what he's learned — the hard way a
 nd the smart way — about where AI actually delivers for early-stage comp
 anies. What use cases are ready today. How to think about capital needs di
 fferently when you can delegate execution to agents instead of headcount. 
 And how to move faster without losing the thing that makes a startup worth
  building in the first place.\n\nThe opportunity in front of founders righ
 t now is the highest level of leverage in 30 years of technology cycles. T
 his session is about how to use it.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/all-things-ai-live/events/314147027/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260406T133731Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T133731Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
