BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/robert-rauschenberg-black-mountain-college-and-the-spreads"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs,Lectures & Talks
DESCRIPTION:Celebrating the centennial of American artist Robert Rauschenbe
 rg’s birth\, this program brings together two lectures that examine distinc
 t moments in the artist’s career. One focuses on Rauschenberg’s time at the
  experimental Black Mountain College\, where his studies with Josef Albers 
 and collaborations with fellow artists shaped key approaches to postwar Ame
 rican art. The other considers Rauschenberg’s lesser-known Spread works fro
 m the 1970s\, including Credit Blossom (Spread) in the collection of the NC
 MA.\n\nRather than tracing a single narrative\, the program places these mo
 ments side by side\, offering focused perspectives on Rauschenberg’s workin
 g methods\, materials\, and artistic concerns across different periods of h
 is career. Speakers include Jeff Arnal\, executive director of the Black Mo
 untain College Museum + Arts Center\, and Sarah Roberts\, who is currently 
 the senior director of curatorial affairs at the Joan Mitchell Foundation a
 nd formerly served as the primary author and editor of the Robert Rauschenb
 erg Research Project and co-curated the 2017–18 retrospective Robert Rausch
 enberg: Erasing the Rules.
DTEND:20260422T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030452Z
DTSTART:20260422T220000Z
GEO:35.807856;-78.703922
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Robert Rauschenberg: Black Mountain College and the Spreads
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52365774536397
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/robert-rauschenberg-black-mountain-col
 lege-and-the-spreads
END:VEVENT
