BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/gallery-walk-joe-coxs-artwork-at-the-d-h-hill-jr-library"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Community Events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Gregg Museum and the NC State University Libraries for
  a gallery walk featuring recently installed artworks created by Joe Cox.\n
 \nBrief remarks will be given by:\n\n› Sara Segerlin\, Gregg Museum Directo
 r and Chair of NC State’s Public Art Committee\n› Sandra Varry\, Head\, Spe
 cial Collections Research Center\, NC State University Libraries\n› Patrick
  Deaton\, Associate Director\, Learning Spaces and Capital Management\, NC 
 State University Libraries\n\nRemarks will be followed by a self-guided gal
 lery walk through the Hill Library’s Ground Floor reading room\, concluding
  at the Color Wall\, located on the second floor of the Hill Library.\n\nSe
 lected items from the Special Collections Resource Center will also be on d
 isplay.\n\nJoe Cox (1915–1997) was a foundational figure in the history of 
 NC State’s College of Design and a nationally respected artist and educator
 . As a painter\, muralist\, and longtime faculty member\, Cox helped shape 
 the college’s early interdisciplinary ethos—bridging fine art\, architectur
 e\, and design. His work is known for its modernist sensibility\, strong co
 mpositional structure\, and engagement with regional and civic themes. Cox’
 s legacy lives on through artworks held by the NC State University Librarie
 s and installed across campus\, reflecting the university’s longstanding co
 mmitment to integrating art into academic and public spaces.\n\nOne of Cox’
 s most notable public artworks in Raleigh is Color Wall\, a kinetic light s
 culpture installed in 1972 inside the D.H. Hill Jr. Library. The work combi
 nes colored spotlights and metal vanes to create shifting patterns of light
  and color—visible from the street at night—and remains a landmark example 
 of mid-century public art at NC State.\n\nPlease RSVP by April 24.
DTEND:20260427T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260427T220000Z
GEO:35.787562;-78.669711
LOCATION:D.H. Hill Jr. Library\, Ground Floor Reading Room
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Gallery Walk: Joe Cox’s artwork at the D. H. Hill Jr. Library
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52550680633703
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/gallery-walk-joe-coxs-artwork-at-the-d-
 h-hill-jr-library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/the-art-and-science-of-plant-care"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Community Events
DESCRIPTION:Caring for plants is both an art and a science — part intuition
 \, part know-how. Every gardener\, from beginner to expert\, faces the same
  essential questions: When should I prune? How much should I water? What’s 
 the best way to plant\, fertilize or repot? In this class\, Bryce Lane will
  bring decades of horticultural expertise to demystify these everyday tasks
 \, showing you not just what to do but why it works.\n\nOver eight weeks\, 
 you’ll explore the fundamental practices that keep gardens thriving\, learn
 ing how to perform each one with confidence and purpose. You’ll uncover the
  science behind good technique — understanding how soil\, water\, nutrients
  and plant biology interact — while also developing the practical judgment 
 that comes only with experience.\n\nEach session will focus on one key aspe
 ct of plant care\, building a complete toolkit for growing healthier\, more
  resilient plants in any garden setting.
DTEND:20260428T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030231Z
DTSTART:20260427T223000Z
GEO:35.794251;-78.699671
LOCATION:JC Raulston Arboretum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:The Art and Science of Plant Care
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52072165587831
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/the-art-and-science-of-plant-care
END:VEVENT
