BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/in-irons-american-prisoners-of-war-1775-1783"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:During the American War of Independence\, many patriots who ser
 ved on land and sea found themselves as prisoners of war. Some were in Brit
 ish prison camps while others were held aboard British prison ships. Join M
 aritime History Curator David Bennett as he details the captivity of North 
 Carolinians and other American patriots\, as well as daring escapes and mar
 itime routes to freedom.\n\nThis program is part of the museum’s Maritime H
 eritage Lecture Series\, informal lectures focused on North Carolina’s rich
  maritime history\, coastal environment\, and culture.  Programs are offere
 d select Thursdays at noon. The lectures are held in the museum auditorium 
 and streamed via Zoom. Admission is free\, and registration is not required
  for the in-person program. Visit ncmaritimemuseumbeaufort.com/virtual to s
 ign up to receive the Zoom links. Programs are also posted to the museum’s 
 YouTube channel.
DTEND:20260430T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030453Z
DTSTART:20260430T160000Z
GEO:34.717841;-76.666223
LOCATION:North Carolina Maritime Museum in Beaufort
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:In Irons: American Prisoners of War\, 1775-1783
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52427732695526
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/in-irons-american-prisoners-of-war-177
 5-1783
END:VEVENT
