CREATED:20260313T175229Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260313T175229Z
UID:10001343-1777806000-1777863600@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Spring Black Neighborhood Walking Tour
DESCRIPTION:Put some spring in your step as you explore Raleigh’s historic and influential Black neighborhood\, the Third Ward\, just around Shaw University\, a wonderful place full of culture\, business\, and learning. \nBe sure to register to join in the fun! Saturday tour times are 10 a.m. and 2 p.m.\, and Sunday tour time 2 p.m. \nDates & Times\nSaturdays and Sundays\, March 21 – June 21\nSaturdays\, 10 a.m. & 2 p.m.\nSundays\, 2 p.m. \nAges: All\nCost: $10 per adult / $5 per child (5- 17)\nRegister on RecLink
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/spring-black-neighborhood-walking-tour/2026-05-03/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/pope-tours.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-county-public-library-main-branch-statesville"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Iredell County Public Library Commemorates 250 Years of Freedom
  with Year-Long Exhibit Series\n\nThe Iredell County Public Library will ho
 st a series of four local history exhibits throughout 2026 as part of Ameri
 ca 250\, the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Indepen
 dence. The inaugural exhibit\, Visions of Freedom\, will open to the public
  on January 12 on the Main floor of the Statesville branch library.\n\nVisi
 ons of Freedom will focus on highlighting local landmarks\, Revolutionary e
 ra residents\, and important social movements that not only shaped the nati
 on\, but the Iredell County community. This free exhibit will offer a blend
  of information\, images\, and engaging interactive activities designed to 
 appeal to visitors of all ages.\n\nFor more details about the exhibit serie
 s and upcoming local history events\, please visit our website at https://i
 redell.lib.nc.us or contact Shellie Taylor at michelle.taylor@iredellcounty
 nc.gov\n\nStatesville Library Hours: M-Th 8am-8pm\, F & Sat 9am-6pm
DTEND:20260504T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260503T120000Z
GEO:35.787463;-80.88791
LOCATION:Iredell County Public Library\, Main level
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Visions of Freedom\, Exhibit #1 (Iredell County Public Library: Mai
 n Branch-Statesville)
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51764560177208
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-c
 ounty-public-library-main-branch-statesville
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_cb2ajgfjpk6bf9gifg6kg2hn1s
SUMMARY:Crank Arm Sunday High Noon Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260503T123000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031317Z
UID:5lnod5e90gsovdq15maroljfh1@google.com__20260503
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20240927T182121Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><p>It's a faster paced and longer ride!</p><p>On Sundays w
 e cycle 20ish miles and the journey lasts roughly 1.5 hours depending on t
 he route. We're rolling roughly at 14-18mph. There is a leader but If you 
 want to go faster GO FOR IT. There will be limited support on this ride. T
 he group will start and finish at Crank Arm. Hang out and enjoy a beer aft
 er.</p><p>Don't forget your helmet.</p><p>Lets have fun and be safe!<br><b
 r></p><p>more info: <a href="https://www.meetup.com/crank-arm-cycling-runn
 ing-yoga/events/303334626/?eventOrigin=group_calendar">https://www.meetup.
 com/crank-arm-cycling-running-yoga/events/303334626/?eventOrigin=group_cal
 endar</a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240927T182121Z
LOCATION:Crank Arm Brewing Company\, 319 W Davie St\, Raleigh\, NC 27601\,
  USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Triangle Cycling
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/village-of-pinehurst-ncdncr-america-250-exhibits"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Education Programs,Youth & Family A
 ctivities
DESCRIPTION:The Village of Pinehurst will be displaying two of the NC Depar
 tment of Natural & Cultural Resources exhibits throughout 2026.\n\n"Forging
  a Nation" will be on display at the Cannon Park Community Center\, 210 Rat
 tlesnake Trail\, Pinehurst\, NC 28374.\n\n"People of Colonial North Carolin
 a" will be on display at Assembly Hall\, 395 Magnolia Rd.\, Pinehurst\, NC 
 28374.\n\nThe Given Memorial Library & Tufts Archives (150 Cherokee Road\, 
 Pinehurst\, NC 28374) will also have smaller versions of the exhibits on di
 splay throughout the year and will rotate between the different exhibit sub
 jects periodically.
DTEND:20260503T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260503T123000Z
