X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Performances
DESCRIPTION:North Carolina singer Laura Gonzqui was born in Venezuela. Her 
 Latin-fusion sound incorporates jazz\, soul\, blues\, salsa and world music
 . Noted for her performances at multiple renowned festivals\, she enchants 
 audiences with her rich vocals and dynamic presence. Gonzqui is making her 
 second appearance at the LIVE at Lake Raleigh series.\n\nThis free\, family
 -friendly concert series on the picturesque shore of Lake Raleigh is a coll
 aboration between NC State LIVE and NC State Centennial and celebrates the 
 unique voices of North Carolina’s extraordinary music scene. Bring your pic
 nic blankets and enjoy dance-inducing music\, delicious food and an amazing
  community gathering.\n\nThe gates will open and food trucks will be on-sit
 e at 5 p.m. Concerts will begin at 6 p.m.
DTEND:20260507T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030232Z
DTSTART:20260507T210000Z
GEO:35.767879;-78.677586
LOCATION:Lake Raleigh
SEQUENCE:0
