BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/bald-eagle-search-paddle-with-two-sisters-adventure-company-9562"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:
DESCRIPTION:Join Two Sisters Adventure Company for a Bald Eagle Search Padd
 le at Jordan Lake State Recreation Area\, hosted on select dates throughout
  2026. Jordan Lake is one of the best Bald Eagle viewing locations in the r
 egion. You will paddle past multiple nesting areas in search of our majesti
 c national bird. While sightings are not guaranteed\, Bald Eagles are most 
 common in the areas they visit. Your guide will help you identify and answe
 r questions about Bald Eagles and other birds in the area. All participants
  should have basic kayaking skills\, due to the duration on the water this 
 trip is considered intermediate. Pre-registration is required. Participants
  will launch from the Farrington Point Access. The trip will last approxima
 tely 4 hours. Trips will take place on the following dates:\n\nThu\, Mar 26
 \, 9am-1pm.\nSun\, Apr 26\, 8:30am-12:30pm.\nSat\, May 9\, 8am-12pm.\nSat\,
  May 30\, 8am-12pm.\nSun\, Jun 7\, 8am-12pm.\n\nTwo Sisters works with all 
 guests to make trips as accessible as possible. Please contact them with an
 y specific accessibility requests so they can ensure they have all the nece
 ssary equipment and staff. Free parking is available at the Farrington Poin
 t Canoe Launch. No pets are allowed. The cost is $60 per person\, and pre-r
 egistration is required. Single-person kayaks are provided. Participants ag
 es 15 and older are welcome.\n\nThis event is part of our Chatham Celebrate
 s America 250 initiative. See more America 250 events. See more Chatham Spo
 rts Alliance events.\n\nTwo Sisters acknowledges that the land on which thi
 s camp takes place is the ancestral land of the Skaruhreh/Tuscarora\, Lumbe
 e\, Mánu: Yį Įsuwą (Catawba)\, Occaneechi\, Shakori\, and Cheraw Nations. A
 s a part of their mission\, they honor and respect the history and signific
 ance this land holds for these Nations’ past\, present\, and future. To fin
 d out more about the Native People and Lands where you live and recreate\, 
 visit this map.
DTEND:20260509T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260509T120000Z
GEO:35.732693;-79.017178
LOCATION:Jordan Lake State Recreation Area
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Bald Eagle Search Paddle with Two Sisters Adventure Company
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51807551006596
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/bald-eagle-search-paddle-with-two-sist
 ers-adventure-company-9562
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-county-public-library-main-branch-statesville"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Iredell County Public Library Commemorates 250 Years of Freedom
  with Year-Long Exhibit Series\n\nThe Iredell County Public Library will ho
 st a series of four local history exhibits throughout 2026 as part of Ameri
 ca 250\, the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Indepen
 dence. The inaugural exhibit\, Visions of Freedom\, will open to the public
  on January 12 on the Main floor of the Statesville branch library.\n\nVisi
 ons of Freedom will focus on highlighting local landmarks\, Revolutionary e
 ra residents\, and important social movements that not only shaped the nati
 on\, but the Iredell County community. This free exhibit will offer a blend
  of information\, images\, and engaging interactive activities designed to 
 appeal to visitors of all ages.\n\nFor more details about the exhibit serie
 s and upcoming local history events\, please visit our website at https://i
 redell.lib.nc.us or contact Shellie Taylor at michelle.taylor@iredellcounty
 nc.gov\n\nStatesville Library Hours: M-Th 8am-8pm\, F & Sat 9am-6pm
DTEND:20260510T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260509T120000Z
GEO:35.787463;-80.88791
LOCATION:Iredell County Public Library\, Main level
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Visions of Freedom\, Exhibit #1 (Iredell County Public Library: Mai
 n Branch-Statesville)
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51764560183358
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-c
 ounty-public-library-main-branch-statesville
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/village-of-pinehurst-ncdncr-america-250-exhibits"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions,Education Programs,Youth & Family A
 ctivities
DESCRIPTION:The Village of Pinehurst will be displaying two of the NC Depar
 tment of Natural & Cultural Resources exhibits throughout 2026.\n\n"Forging
  a Nation" will be on display at the Cannon Park Community Center\, 210 Rat
 tlesnake Trail\, Pinehurst\, NC 28374.\n\n"People of Colonial North Carolin
 a" will be on display at Assembly Hall\, 395 Magnolia Rd.\, Pinehurst\, NC 
 28374.\n\nThe Given Memorial Library & Tufts Archives (150 Cherokee Road\, 
 Pinehurst\, NC 28374) will also have smaller versions of the exhibits on di
 splay throughout the year and will rotate between the different exhibit sub
 jects periodically.
DTEND:20260509T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260509T123000Z
