BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-county-public-library-main-branch-statesville"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
DESCRIPTION:Iredell County Public Library Commemorates 250 Years of Freedom
  with Year-Long Exhibit Series\n\nThe Iredell County Public Library will ho
 st a series of four local history exhibits throughout 2026 as part of Ameri
 ca 250\, the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Indepen
 dence. The inaugural exhibit\, Visions of Freedom\, will open to the public
  on January 12 on the Main floor of the Statesville branch library.\n\nVisi
 ons of Freedom will focus on highlighting local landmarks\, Revolutionary e
 ra residents\, and important social movements that not only shaped the nati
 on\, but the Iredell County community. This free exhibit will offer a blend
  of information\, images\, and engaging interactive activities designed to 
 appeal to visitors of all ages.\n\nFor more details about the exhibit serie
 s and upcoming local history events\, please visit our website at https://i
 redell.lib.nc.us or contact Shellie Taylor at michelle.taylor@iredellcounty
 nc.gov\n\nStatesville Library Hours: M-Th 8am-8pm\, F & Sat 9am-6pm
DTEND:20260512T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260511T120000Z
GEO:35.787463;-80.88791
LOCATION:Iredell County Public Library\, Main level
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Visions of Freedom\, Exhibit #1 (Iredell County Public Library: Mai
 n Branch-Statesville)
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51764560185408
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/visions-of-freedom-exhibit-1-iredell-c
 ounty-public-library-main-branch-statesville
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Raleigh Ai Machine Learning And Computer Vision Meetup": "https://www.meetup.com/raleigh-ai-machine-learning-and-computer-vision-meetup/events/314090327/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_raleigh_ai_machine_learning_and_computer_vision_meetup
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Raleigh AI, ML & Computer Vision
UID:event_314090327@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260407T031311Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260511T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260511T140000
SUMMARY:May 11 - Best of 3DV 2026
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh AI\, Machine Learning and Computer Vision Meetup\nWelc
 ome to the Best of 3DV series\, your virtual pass to some of the groundbre
 aking research\, insights\, and innovations that defined this year’s con
 ference. Live streaming from the authors to you.\n\n**Date\, Time and Loca
 tion**\n\nMay 11\, 2026\n9AM Pacific\nOnline. **[Register for Zoom!](https
 ://voxel51.com/events/best-of-3dv-2026-may-11-2026)**\n\n**Navigating a 3D
  Vision Conference with VLMs and Embeddings**\n\nAttending the 3D Vision C
 onference means confronting 177 accepted papers across 3.5 days\, far more
  than any one person can absorb. Skimming titles the night before isn't en
 ough.\n\nThis talk shows how to build a systematic\, interactive map of an
  entire conference using modern open-source tools. We load all 177 papers 
 from 3DV 2026 (full PDF page images plus metadata) into a FiftyOne grouped
  dataset. We then run three annotation passes using Qwen3.5-9B on each cov
 er page: topic classification\, author affiliation extraction\, and projec
 t page detection. Document embeddings from Jina v4 are computed across all
  3\,019 page images\, pooled to paper-level vectors\, and fed into FiftyOn
 e Brain for UMAP visualization\, similarity search\, representativeness sc
 oring\, and uniqueness scoring.\n\nThe result is an interactive dataset yo
 u can query\, filter\, and explore in the FiftyOne App. Sort by uniqueness
  to find distinctive work\, filter by topic and sort by representativeness
  to understand each research area\, and cross-reference with scheduling me
 tadata to build a personal agenda.\n\nI demonstrate the end-to-end pipelin
 e and discuss design decisions regarding grouped datasets\, reasoning mode
 l output parsing\, and embedding pooling strategies.\n\n*About the Speaker
 *\n\n[Harpreet Sahota](https://www.linkedin.com/in/harpreetsahota204/) is 
 a hacker-in-residence and machine learning engineer with a passion for dee
 p learning and generative AI. He’s got a deep interest in VLMs\, Visual 
 Agents\, Document AI\, and Physical AI.\n\n**Seeing Through Clutter: Struc
 tured 3D Scene Reconstruction via Iterative Object Removal**\n\nWe present
  SeeingThroughClutter\, a method for reconstructing structured 3D represen
 tations from single images by segmenting and modeling objects individually
 . Prior approaches rely on intermediate tasks such as semantic segmentatio
 n and depth estimation\, which often underperform in complex scenes\, part
 icularly in the presence of occlusion and clutter.\n\nWe address this by i
 ntroducing an iterative object removal and reconstruction pipeline that de
 composes complex scenes into a sequence of simpler subtasks. Using VLMs as
  orchestrators\, foreground objects are removed one at a time via detectio
 n\, segmentation\, object removal\, and 3D fitting. We show that removing 
 objects allows for cleaner segmentations of subsequent objects\, even in h
 ighly occluded scenes. Our method requires no task-specific training and b
 enefits directly from ongoing advances in foundation models. We demonstrat
 e state-of-the-art robustness on 3D-Front and ADE20K datasets.\n\n*About t
 he Speaker*\n\n[Rio Aguina-Kang](https://www.linkedin.com/in/raguinak/) is
  currently a Machine Learning Engineer at Drafted AI\, a startup focused o
 n generative architecture. He has previously worked at Adobe Research\, Br
 own Visual Computing\, and the Stanford Institute for Human-Centered Artif
 icial Intelligence. He is broadly interested in building systems that let 
 users generate and control visual content through structured representatio
 ns that reflect their intent.\n\n**Physical Realistic 4D Generation**\n\nG
 enerating dynamic 3D content that moves and deforms over time is a key fro
 ntier in visual computing\, with applications in VR/AR\, robotics\, and di
 gital humans. In this talk\, I present our series of works on physically r
 ealistic 4D generation: from neural surface deformation with explicit velo
 city fields (ICLR 2025) to our 4Deform framework for robust shape interpol
 ation (CVPR 2025). Both methods use implicit neural representations with p
 hysically constrained velocity fields that enforce volume preservation\, s
 patial smoothness\, and geometric consistency. I will also introduce TwoSq
 uared (3DV 2026\, oral)\, which achieves full 4D generation from just two 
 2D image pairs — demonstrating a practical path toward controllable\, ph
 ysically plausible 4D content creation.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[⁠Lu S
 ang ](https://www.linkedin.com/in/lu-sang-tum/)is a PhD researcher in Comp
 uter Vision at TU Munich (Prof. Daniel Cremers)\, specializing in 3D/4D re
 construction\, neural implicit surfaces\, and inverse rendering\, with ser
 veral publications at top venues including CVPR\, ICLR\, and ECCV. She is 
 currently a research intern at Google XR in Zurich. With a strong mathemat
 ical foundation and a track record spanning photometric stereo to 4D gener
 ation\, she brings both theoretical depth and hands-on engineering to cutt
 ing-edge visual computing research.\n\n**Finding NeMO: A Geometry-Aware Re
 presentation of Template Views for Few-Shot Perception**\n\nHow can we use
  and perceive objects without training a new model given only a few images
 ? We present NeMO\, a novel object representation that allows 6DoF object 
 pose estimation\, detection and segmentation given only a hand full of RGB
  images of an unknown object.\n\n*About the Speaker*\n\n[Sebastian Jung](h
 ttps://www.linkedin.com/me?trk=p_mwlite_feed-secondary_nav) studied physic
 s at the LMU munich. He started his PhD in Computer Science at the german 
 aerospace center (DLR) in 2025 and focuses on object centric few shot perc
 eption with a focus on robotic applications. Additionally\, he's a student
  researcher at google\, focusing on computer vision algorithms for XR.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/raleigh-ai-machine-learning-and-compu
 ter-vision-meetup/events/314090327/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260402T155023Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260402T155023Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
