BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/adult-nights-social-in-the-shire"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Special Site Programs
DESCRIPTION:Gather up your Fellowship as the Museum becomes Middle Earth fo
 r a night. Lay siege to Gondor\, dance with dragons and show off your Tolki
 en trivia at this adults 21+ event.\n\nEnjoy a unique opportunity to experi
 ence the Museum at night while exploring the uncensored side of science. Th
 e event features interactive science stations\, music\, games\, local enter
 tainment and special activities. Beer\, wine\, themed cocktails and food wi
 ll be available for purchase. Costumes encouraged (but not required).\n\nTi
 ckets: $25\; $15 Members. You must be 21 years or older to attend. A photo 
 ID is required for entry.\n\nCOSTUME POLICY\n\nGuests wearing masks must re
 move them during check-in. They can then wear them during the event.Footwea
 r is required.Outfits should not contain elements that resemble or could be
  mistaken for a real weapon.We reserve the right to refuse a guest wearing 
 a costume deemed offensive or unsafe.Any face or body paint must not obscur
 e an attendee’s identity.
DTEND:20260516T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260515T223000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Adult Nights: Social in the Shire
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52401425680171
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/adult-nights-social-in-the-shire
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/astronomy-3145"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation,Nature & Wildlife Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join us and the Crystal Coast Stargazers at the beach access / 
 bathhouse parking area to view space through a telescope and learn more abo
 ut our universe.\n\nThis event is dependent on clear weather and may be can
 celed due to rain or heavy cloud cover. If you have a telescope\, feel free
  to bring it. Pets are not permitted at this program. \n\nIf you are not se
 tting up equipment for observations we ask that you park in the west parkin
 g lot as you first enter\, then walk across to the east lot for the program
 .  This helps reduce the amount of bright lights in the observation area fr
 om headlights. \n\n \n\nPhoto by P. Terry: Star trails over a cannon at For
 t Macon State Park
DTEND:20260516T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260516T000000Z
GEO:34.696366;-76.684506
LOCATION:Fort Macon State Park\, Beach Access / Bathhouse Parking Area (Pic
 nic Park Dr.)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Astronomy
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51922255996240
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/astronomy-3145
