X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/fiber-frolic-at-hickory-ridge-history-museum"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Festivals & Fairs
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate five years of fiber arts at the Fifth Annual Fiber Fr
 olic\, held at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone\, NC. Fiber\, crafters
 \, and curious families all come together for a full day of hands-on demons
 trations and traditional textile arts.\n\nExplore the craft traditions that
  sustained mountain communities for generations through live demonstrations
  and interactive activities\, including spinning\, wool carding\, weaving\,
  natural dyeing\, and knitting and crocheting. Whether you are a lifelong f
 iber artist or picking up a drop spindle for the very first time\, the Fibe
 r Frolic is a welcoming\, all-ages event with something to discover at ever
 y cabin.\n\nFree admission. All ages welcome. No registration required.
DTEND:20260516T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030454Z
DTSTART:20260516T150000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
