BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/new-sba-7a-manufacturers-access-to-revolving-credit-marc-loans-webinar"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC State University
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
DESCRIPTION:Join NC State Industry Expansion Solutions for a webinar that w
 ill focus on the Small Business Administration's (SBA) new 7(a) Manufacture
 rs’ Access to Revolving Credit (MARC) Loans.\n\nMARC is SBA’s first-ever lo
 an program dedicated to supporting America’s small manufacturers\, which ma
 ke up 98% of all U.S. manufacturers. The program will offer working capital
  for small businesses engaged in manufacturing and is specifically designed
  to provide maximum flexibility and minimal red tape.\n\nMARC complements t
 he SBA’s core 7(a) and 504 loan programs\, providing a flexible new line of
  credit to manufacturers and lenders. MARC loans can be used in combination
  with SBA and conventional commercial loans\, making it a potent new tool i
 n support of SBA's effort to reshore American industrial dominance.
DTEND:20260611T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030232Z
DTSTART:20260611T140000Z
LOCATION:
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY: Webinar: 7(a) Manufacturers’ Access to Revolving Credit Loans
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52073087340714
URL:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/new-sba-7a-manufacturers-access-to-revo
 lving-credit-marc-loans-webinar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours,Exhibitions
DESCRIPTION:March 14 – August 23\, 2026\n\nIn the ultimate battle for survi
 val\, every animal has a plan.\n\nExplore the striking ways nature fights b
 ack in “Staying Alive\,” featuring 17 live animals from around the world wi
 th unbelievable self-defense strategies. Come face to face with trippy toad
 s\, armored armadillos\, a two-toed sloth and more.\n\nDiscover how these d
 efenders deploy an amazing arsenal of high-fashion camouflage and mimicry\,
  specialized armor and advanced chemical warfare – like stink bombs\, caboo
 se cannons and smoke screens – to hide in plain sight\, stand their ground 
 or even drop a limb and make a run for it. Enjoy live animal encounters\, l
 arger-than-life sculptures\, 3D tactile experiences and interactive program
 s.\n\nPerfect for families and animal enthusiasts of all ages. Offered in E
 nglish & Spanish.
DTEND:20260611T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030455Z
DTSTART:20260611T140000Z
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Staying Alive 
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52207082982654
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/staying-alive
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/siler-city-history-club"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join the Chatham County Historical Association for the Siler Ci
 ty History Club on every second Thursday of the month\, 10:30am-11:30am at 
 First Baptist Church. The Chatham County Historical Association needs your 
 help in learning about the rich and colorful history of Siler City! They ha
 ve facts and figures\, but they need to hear your own memories of Siler to 
 really understand one of Chatham County’s most important cities. Come share
  your memories\, stories\, photos\, mementos\, and other Siler City treasur
 es. Light refreshments will be served. This event is free\, and everyone is
  welcome! No registration is required.\n\nThis event takes place indoors. F
 irst Baptist Church in Siler City is ADA-accessible. No pets allowed. Pleas
 e leave your furry friends at home. Free parking is available next to the c
 hurch.\n\nThis event is part of our Chatham Celebrates America 250 initiati
 ve. See more America 250 events. See more events hosted by The Chatham Hist
 orical Association.
DTEND:20260611T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030455Z
DTSTART:20260611T143000Z
GEO:35.726177;-79.463313
LOCATION:First Baptist Church 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Siler City History Club
