BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:PA Stagville & the Roots of Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T113000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031319Z
UID:7dehtdmgg7j2gfbuveugdpnj8g@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T100000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260326T191137Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br><br><br><p><em>Commemorate Independence Day with a rea
 ding of Frederick Douglass' powerful Fourth of July address\, "What to the
  Slave is the Fourth of July." This is a participatory community reading.
  Every year\, 60 volunteers sign up to read passages from the speech in fr
 ont of the slave dwellings at Horton Grove. You may sign up as a reader wh
 en you arrive. </em></p><p><em>Douglass delivered this powerful abolition
 ist speech on July 5\, 1852 at an Independence Day celebration in Rocheste
 r\, New York. Douglass' speech remains one of the most famous abolitionist
  texts in U.S. history. The speech resonates today\, inviting all to refle
 ct on the history of slavery\, freedom\, and the United States' founding i
 deals.</em></p><p><em>Bring a chair or blanket to sit on the grounds. The 
 event will be outdoors at the historic slave quarters at Horton Grove. Att
 endees must walk less than one hundred yards over uneven grass or gravel t
 o reach the reading site. </em></p><p><em>This free event will last about
  1 hour\, with the option to tour the original slave dwellings at Horton G
 rove available afterwards. </em></p>      <br>    <br>WHEN    <br>       
      July 04\, 2026 at 10:00am - 11:30am                <br>    <br>WHERE 
    <br>            Stagville Historic Site<br>                  5828 Old O
 xford Hwy<br>            Durham\, NC 27712<br>            United States<br
 >                  <a href="https://maps.google.com/maps?q=5828+Old+Oxford
 +Hwy\,+Durham\,+NC+27712\,+United+States">Google map and directions</a>   
                <br>    <br>CONTACT    <br>      Ann Rebeck            · <
 a href="mailto:PA@durhampa.org">PA@durhampa.org</a>                  · (9
 19) 682-7777            <br><br><a href="https://www.durhampa.org/stagvill
 e_july4_2026">https://www.durhampa.org/stagville_july4_2026</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260326T191137Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (In Person)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Defend Democracy Saturdays: Downtown Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T113000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031319Z
UID:7vihpmeg1k6esqp5s5vsvq9hfe_R20260110T150000@google.com__20260704
SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20251010T141601Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Saturday 
 from 10am-11:30am with signs to protect our democracy and protest the viol
 ations to our Constitution. We will meet at the YMCA at 218 West Morgan St
 .</p><p>We need to fight for our democracy and stop and prevent future cut
 s that are hurting many. Bring friends! Bring signs that show your concern
  or are a call to action. Please avoid triggering images like swastikas.</
 p><p>See you every Saturday morning engaging drivers &amp\; pedestrians in
  Downtown Durham!</p><p>Please join our Substack:<span> </span><a href="h
 ttps://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy">https
 ://substack.com/profile/115484101-engaged-defenders-4-democracy</a></p><p>
 For more ED4D Mobilize Events:<span> </span><a href="https://www.mobilize
 .us/engagedefendersfordemocracy/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersf
 ordemocracy/</a></p><p><a href="https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfor
 democracy/event/842514/">https://www.mobilize.us/engagedefendersfordemocra
 cy/event/842514/</a> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260108T021307Z
LOCATION:218 W Morgan St\, Durham\, NC\, 27701
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
