X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/fort-fishers-second-world-war"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Reenactments & Living History,Exhi
 bits & Tours,Special Site Programs
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Fort Fisher State Historic Site for our annual\, day
 -long event about the WWII experience at Fort Fisher on October 3rd\, 2026!
 \n\nGeneral admission is FREE\, no tickets required for entry. Doors open a
 t 9:00am and close at 5:00pm. Public programs will be held between 10:00am 
 and 4:00pm.\n\nMore information about these programs will be provided in th
 e coming months. Stay tuned to the NC DNCR Events Calendar and Fort Fisher'
 s social media as we approach October 3!
DTEND:20261003T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030457Z
DTSTART:20261003T140000Z
GEO:33.971637;-77.91773
LOCATION:Fort Fisher Historic Site
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Fort Fisher's Second World War
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51781004638012
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/fort-fishers-second-world-war
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/appalachian-autumn-market-fall-festival"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations,Festivals & Fairs
DESCRIPTION:Step into the beauty of fall at our Appalachian Autumn Market &
  Fall Festival! This family-friendly event\, free to the public\, offers a 
 wonderful array of activities and experiences for all ages.\n\nApple Butter
  Making & 18th-Century Demonstrations: Take a walk through history and lear
 n about the rich traditions of the past with live demonstrations of apple b
 utter making and demonstrations like weaving\, spinning\, blacksmithing\, a
 nd more!\n\nMaker and Food Vendors: Explore a marketplace of creativity and
  flavor with local artisans showcasing their crafts and delectable treats. 
 It's the perfect opportunity to discover unique treasures and savor delicio
 us bites! Get ahead on your holiday shopping!\n\nLive Music and Storytellin
 g: Enjoy local and traditional Appalachian musicians and storytellers live 
 and in-person! Mary Greene\, Orville Hicks\, Diandra Patterson\, and more!\
 n\nHatchet Throwing (Paid Activity): Test your aim and have a blast with ou
 r hatchet-throwing activity. Suitable for ages 14+. It's a fun and exciting
  way for older kids to burn off energy and challenge their skills. And of c
 ourse\, it's just plain fun for adults!\n\nPumpkin Painting (Paid Activity)
 : Unleash your inner artist and transform pumpkins into works of art at our
  painting station. A wonderful activity for all ages!\n\nKid's Costume Cont
 est (Paid Activity): Dress to impress and participate in our costume contes
 t! Prizes await the most creative and spooktacular outfits.\n\nPet Costume 
 Contest (Paid Activity): Don't forget your furry friends! Show off their be
 st costumes and compete for fantastic prizes in our pet costume contest.\n\
 nRaffles: Enter our 50/50 raffle for a chance to win a cash prize. Who does
 n't love that?!\n\nAnd SO MUCH MORE Fall Goodness! Mark your calendar for a
  day filled with autumnal magic\, laughter\, and community spirit. The Appa
 lachian Autumn Market & Fall Festival is an experience you won't want to mi
 ss!
DTEND:20261003T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260407T030457Z
DTSTART:20261003T180000Z
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Appalachian Autumn Market & Fall Festival
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52463233812958
URL:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/appalachian-autumn-market-fall-festiva
 l
END:VEVENT
